<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-McIntosh will accept Merrill bid.</title>
<headline>RTRS-McIntosh will accept Merrill bid.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>McIntosh Securities Ltd said on Monday it would accept the A$1.40 per share takeover offer from New York brokerage firm Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc in the absence of a higher offer.  </p>
<p>&quot;The directors of McIntosh believe that both the value of McIntosh's existing and potential business and McIntosh's contribution to the anticipated benefits to be gained in the merged entity are fairly reflected in the price offered by Merrill Lynch to existing McIntosh shareholders,&quot; McIntosh said.</p>
<p>The offer values McIntosh, which is about 19.9 percent owned by Netherland's Ing Bank at about A$117 million.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
